<!--
    StatusIcon – the 16 × 16 status mark in front of every test (Paper "9c · Running", test list).

    One control, five states (TestState):

        Queued      Running        Passed       Failed       Aborted
          ◌            ◠             ✓            ✕             –
        dashed      blue arc      green disc    red disc     amber disc
        grey ring   turning on    white check   white cross  white dash
                    a pale ring

    Layers, back to front (all share the same 16 × 16 box, only one group is visible at a time):
      1. Halo ...... a soft ring of the result colour, 4 px larger than the icon on every side. Invisible at rest.
                     It breathes once (opacity only, full size from the first frame) when a test fails or aborts.
      2. Queued .... dashed grey ring, 12 px, 1.5 stroke.
      3. Spinner ... pale blue ring (2 px) with a quarter arc in brand blue on top; the whole group turns once every 0.9 s.
      4. Disc ...... solid 14 px circle + a white glyph drawn as a stroke, so it can "write itself".

    Motion (StatusIcon.xaml.cs), played when a test changes state in front of the user or has just finished:
      · the spinner fades out while the disc fades in and settles from 86 % to 100 % size – it never grows from a point
      · the glyph is drawn along its path a moment later: the check from its short leg to its long leg,
        the two strokes of the cross together, the dash from left to right
      · failed and aborted add one slow halo pulse; passed stays calm
    Rows that were already finished when they came into view (scrolling, switching the filter) appear without motion.
    With Windows animations turned off, every state is shown at once.

    Use:  <local:StatusIcon State="{Binding State}" IsFresh="{Binding IsFresh}" />
          <local:StatusIcon State="Running" />
-->
<UserControl x:Class="Conduit.StatusIcon"
             x:Name="Root"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             Width="16" Height="16"
             Focusable="False"
             VerticalAlignment="Center">

    <Grid>

        <!-- 1 · Halo: 24 × 24 around the 16 px box (hence the negative margin). Fill is set per state in code. -->
        <Ellipse x:Name="Halo" Margin="-4" Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False" />

        <!-- 2 · Queued: the test has not started yet. -->
        <Ellipse x:Name="Queued" Width="12" Height="12" Opacity="0"
                 Stroke="{StaticResource Dot}" StrokeThickness="1.5" StrokeDashArray="1.6 1.5" StrokeDashCap="Round" />

        <!-- 3 · Spinner: track + arc. The arc is a quarter circle from 12 to 3 o'clock; the group rotates around its centre. -->
        <Grid x:Name="Spinner" Opacity="0" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
            <Grid.RenderTransform>
                <RotateTransform x:Name="Spin" />
            </Grid.RenderTransform>
            <Ellipse Stroke="{StaticResource BlueRing}" StrokeThickness="2" />
            <Path Data="M8,1 A7,7 0 0 1 15,8" Stroke="{StaticResource Blue}" StrokeThickness="2"
                  StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- 4 · Disc + glyph. The scale transform is only used for the short "settle" when a result arrives. -->
        <Grid x:Name="Disc" Opacity="0" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
            <Grid.RenderTransform>
                <ScaleTransform x:Name="DiscScale" />
            </Grid.RenderTransform>
            <Ellipse x:Name="DiscFill" Width="14" Height="14" />
            <!-- Glyph geometry, thickness and dash length come from the code-behind (one entry per state).
                 Coordinates are in the 16-unit box of the icon. -->
            <Canvas Width="16" Height="16">
                <Path x:Name="Glyph" Stroke="White" StrokeThickness="1.7"
                      StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" StrokeLineJoin="Round" />
            </Canvas>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
